      {
        "id": "the-sound-that-told-the-owner-to-stop-driving-immediately",
        "title": "The sound that told the owner to stop driving immediately.",
        "description": "The owner first noticed a brief rattling noise on cold starts around 85,000 miles. The noise lasted approximately two seconds after ignition, then disappeared. The car drove normally otherwise - no loss of power, no warning lights.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/tfsi-death-rattle-12.png",
            "alt": "Audi 2.0 TFSI death rattle sound visualisation - 2-second warning signal caught in time",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What they thought"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "\"Maybe it's just the engine settling.\""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil level was fine. No warning lights. Car drove normally."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What it actually was"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Spring-loaded tensioner failing"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The original design can fail without warning. When it fails, the chain jumps and pistons collide with valves."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The intervention"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Friend recognised it"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "\"That's the death rattle. Don't drive it. Get it towed.\" The owner listened."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The 2.0 TFSI (EA888 Gen2) is equipped with a timing chain tensioner that uses a spring-loaded design rather than oil pressure alone. According to workshop consensus [INDUSTRY ESTIMATE], the original tensioner design can fail without warning."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Timeline"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-sound-that-told-the-owner-to-stop-driving-immediately",
          "order": 1
